# SYNTHETIC capture log -- 04-hardware.md §4 Phase-0 deliverable.
#
# HONEST NOTE: this log was hand-crafted, NOT captured from physical hardware. No real serial
# scale or substitute device was available in this development environment (Phase-0 spike NO-GO,
# see docs/hardware/scale-protocol-notes.md). It exists purely so the SerialScale replay test
# (plan §7, "no hardware, CI-safe") has real bytes to exercise `ScaleProtocol.feed()` against.
#
# Format: <ISO timestamp>\tHEX=<raw frame bytes, hex, including the CRLF delimiter>\tASCII=<frame text>
# Frames follow the plan's continuous-generic example: "ST,GS, 1.234 kg\r\n" (ST/US = stable/
# unstable, GS = gross weight, value in kg). Cadence ~100-120ms/frame, mimicking a device that
# streams continuously (no poll command) while an item is placed, ramps, and settles.
#
# Scenario: an item is placed on the scale; it ramps unstable through a few readings, then settles
# stable at 0.842 kg (842 g) and holds.
